# Signal Node.js Control Plane Rules (`services/**`)

Skills: `signal-nodejs-bff-control-plane`, `signal-byo-git-and-vault`, `signal-universal-parts-registry`, `signal-cad-cam-plm-ops`, `signal-release-deploy-topology`, `signal-security-isolation-audit`.

## 1. Architecture & Clean Structure
- Node.js 22 LTS + strict TypeScript (`strict: true`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes: true`). Keep services (`api-gateway`, `identity-org`, `project-catalog`, `parts-registry`, `plm-ops`, `vcs-connector`, `vcs-auditor`, `session-broker`, `sftp-egress`, `audit-service`) 100% horizontally stateless in `pool-api` alongside native Envoy `signal-engine-bridge` zero-copy relay.
- Keep files `<= 300 LOC` with 3-line `/** Module / Invariants / Spec */` headers. Strictly separate `routes/`, `handlers/`, `policies/` (`@Require*` guards), `repos/` (RLS SQL), and `types/` (build-time generated contract DTOs).
- Generate ALL API & gRPC types at build time from `contracts/` (`longAsBigint: true`) — NEVER hand-edit or commit generated stubs, and NEVER cast 64-bit `bigint` IDs/epochs to JS `number`.
- Never execute EDA physics, SPICE, B-Rep CAD, CNC/3D slicing, DRC/LVS, routing, or Gerber/GDSII/STEP/G-code/3MF generation in Node.js.

## 2. Fail-Closed Auth, Anti-Enumeration & RLS
- Every route MUST declare an explicit fail-closed `@Require*` authorization decorator; unannotated routes fail boot in tests/startup.
- Return **uniform `404 Not Found`** whenever a caller lacks access to an org, project, sub-project, or resource UUID (never leak `403` vs `404` existence!).
- Every PostgreSQL query MUST execute inside a transaction setting `SET LOCAL app.org_id` / `app.user_id` under a `NOBYPASSRLS` role; name migrations `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_<ag|cursor>_<slug>.sql`.
- Auth flows use top-level `/auth/*` PKCE/SAML redirects upgrading `5 min` `SameSite=Lax` state cookies into `__Host-signal_session` (`HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict`) + `Sec-Fetch-Site` guards.
- Enforce `Idempotency-Key` on all mutating endpoints.

## 3. Step-Up 2FA, Anti-SSRF & Fail-Closed Tier-0 Audit
- Require fresh Step-Up 2FA (WebAuthn passkey or Redis-nonce-burned TOTP — single-use per 30s window) for VCS credentials, Access Review revocations, ECN/21 CFR Part 11 sign-offs, and Authorized SFTP targets/releases.
- Route ALL outbound customer Git/SFTP/webhook calls through socket-pinned `signal-egress-proxy` (zero direct outbound HTTP/TCP sockets from BFF services; treat incoming Git webhooks as untrusted dirty hints only).
- Tier-0 security mutations (`SFTP Release`, `VCS Credentials`, `Access Revocation`, `Break-Glass`, `BYOK Edit`) MUST commit synchronously to the **3x Quorum Audit Outbox** (fail-closed `503` if unavailable) using pseudonymous IDs (zero raw PII in WORM Merkle logs).
- Strictly forbid `child_process.exec`, `eval`, `new Function`, raw secret logging (wrap in `Redacted<T>`), and any `/export`, `/download`, or `/print` endpoint.

## 4. Verification Before Commit
Run `pnpm --filter @signal/services lint`, `typecheck`, `test --run`, and `pnpm audit --ignore-scripts`.

## 5. Dev Response & Anti-Hallucination
Reply in **2–3 sentences max** (`Issue -> Fix -> Observed check result`). Verify route/schema/DB symbols via `rg`/`view_file` before editing; never claim green without observed exit code `0`.
